# CODEOWNERS — who signs off on a pull request before it lands on main.
#
# Listed here are ALL the collaborators with write access to the repo, not an
# on-call subset. The reason is that `require_code_owner_reviews` demands the
# approval of an owner WHO IS NOT THE AUTHOR: the shorter the list, the easier
# it is for the only available owner to be exactly the person who opened the
# pull request, and then nothing lands. With the whole list, any author is
# always left with six people who can unblock them.
#
# Requirement to appear here: write access to the repo — GitHub silently
# ignores an owner who does not have it, and the rule quietly stops having any
# effect. If someone joins or leaves the collaborator list, this file goes
# stale on its own: there is nothing that keeps it in sync.
#
# This list is only half of the gate. The other half lives in the branch
# protection of `main` and is NOT in any file of this repo: required `ci`
# check, one approval, and `enforce_admins`.

